Nor did I compare a priceless stone with her,
for all gold in her sight is a little sand,
and silver will be reckoned as clay before her.

Nor did I compare a priceless stone with her,
for all gold in her sight is a little sand,
and silver will be reckoned as clay before her.

And if anyone loves righteousness,
her labors are virtues;
for she teaches self-control and understanding,
righteousness and courage;
nothing in life is more useful for human beings than these.

And if anyone longs for wide experience,
she knows ancient things and infers what is to come;
she understands turns of speech and solutions of riddles;
she knows signs and wonders beforehand,
and the outcomes of seasons and times.

You who thirst, go to the water;
and you who have no silver, go and buy wine and rich food,
and drink without silver or price.

They rise as far as the heavens
and descend as far as the deeps;
their soul melted in evils.
